**Article 1. PURPOSE**

The purpose of this Agreement is to define the terms and conditions under which the Disclosing Party may communicate certain confidential information to the Receiving Party, strictly in connection with {{ purpose_type }}.

---

**Article 2. DEFINITIONS**

“Confidential Information”  shall mean any and all non-public information, whether tangible or intangible, in any form or medium (written, oral, electronic, visual, etc.), disclosed by the Disclosing Party to the Receiving Party, directly or indirectly, for the purpose of the Project, including but not limited to: [contracts, memorandum, notes, reports, analysis, studies, charts, policies, legal opinions, know-how, technologies, and any other proprietary information.]

“Representatives” means, with respect to a Party, any employee, director, officer, agent, consultant, advisor (including legal counsel, accountants, and financial advisors), or affiliate of a Party. The Receiving Party shall be legally responsible for any breach of this Agreement by any of its Representatives.

"Third Party" means any individuals, entities with legal personality or not, organizations of any form or any other entity, which is not a Party to this Agreement, nor a Representative of any of the Parties.

---

**Article 3. USE OF CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION**

**3.1 Permitted Use**

The Receiving Party shall use the Confidential Information solely for the purpose of the Project at the exclusion of any other purpose. The Receiving Party shall not disclose, disseminate, or otherwise make available any Confidential Information to any Third Party for the duration of the confidentiality obligations as defined by this Agreement.

**3.2 Use of confidential information and standard of care**

The Receiving Party shall protect Confidential Information with the same standard of care that it applies to protect its own proprietary information of a similar nature, but in no event shall such care be less than a high standard of care. 
The Receiving Party commits to take all necessary steps to safeguard the Confidential Information from loss, theft, unauthorized access, or destruction, and to ensure that Representatives are aware of the confidential nature of such information and are bound by obligations of confidentiality no less restrictive than those set forth in this Agreement.
In the event of entrusting the Receiving Party with the processing of any personal data pursuant to  privacy and personal data protection laws, the Receiving Party agrees to process the received personal data only for the purpose of the Project and commits to comply with the privacy and personal data protection law provisions, in particular such Party is obliged to:

a) safeguard all entrusted personal data,

b) process the personal data in accordance with the privacy law and protect them against disclosure during the whole time of the Agreement being in force and after its termination. 

---

**Article 4. LEGALLY REQUIRED DISCLOSURE**

Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Receiving Party may disclose Confidential Information if such disclosure is required by a binding law, a court order, or by governmental regulation, provided that:

a) the Receiving Party promptly notifies the Disclosing Party in writing of such requirement prior to the disclosure, to the extent legally permissible;

b) the Receiving Party cooperates with the Disclosing Party, at the Disclosing Party's expense, in seeking a protective order or other appropriate remedy to prevent or limit such disclosure; and

c) the Receiving Party discloses only that portion of the Confidential Information that is legally required and takes all reasonable steps to ensure that the Confidential Information so disclosed is treated with confidentiality. 

---

**Article 5. EXCLUSIONS FROM CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION**

The obligations of confidentiality under this Agreement shall not apply to any information that the Receiving Party can demonstrate:

a) was already in the public domain

b) was rightfully received from a Third Party without restriction on disclosure and without breach of any obligation of confidentiality;

c) was already in the lawful possession of the Receiving Party prior to its disclosure by the Disclosing Party, free from any obligation of confidentiality.

---

**Article 6. DURATION**

The provisions of this Agreement shall terminate on the earlier of: (i) {{ duration }} months from the Effective Date; and (ii) the termination date of the Project as mutually agreed by the Parties.

Notwithstanding the foregoing, confidentiality obligations set forth in this Agreement shall survive the Agreement's termination for maximum period permitted by the law, however not shorter than 5 years from its termination.

---

**Article 7. CONDITIONS OF TERMINATION**

All information provided by the Disclosing Party shall remain the property of the Disclosing Party. Depending on the instructions given by the Disclosing Party, the Receiving Party commits to (i) destroy and provide for a certificate of destruction to the Disclosing Party, or (ii) return all Confidential Information to the Disclosing Party, in both case within fifteen (15) calendar days of written demand by the Disclosing Party.

---

**Article 8. RESPONSIBILITY**

The Receiving Party shall be fully liable for damages to the Disclosing Party for any harm or damage caused to the Disclosing Party or the Disclosing Party's customers or any business partners due to a breach of the terms of this Agreement, including for any harm or damage caused by the Receiving Party’s Representatives.  
Damages may not be the sole adequate remedy for a breach of this Agreement and/or breach of confidence, and the Disclosing Party may be entitled to seek remedies of injunction, specific performance and other equitable relief for a threatened or actual breach of this Agreement and/or breach of confidence, at the Receiving Party’s expense. 

---

**Article 9. NON-SOLICITATION**

During the term of this Agreement and for a period of 12 months following its termination, neither Party shall, directly or indirectly, solicit or entice away any employee of the other Party who has been involved on the Project. 

---

